{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1388701-the-dreaming-freeholds-and-bedlam","id":1388701,"title":"The Dreaming, Freeholds, and Bedlam","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-15T09:25:14-07:00","id":1388701,"title":"The Dreaming, Freeholds, and Bedlam","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> Hope I find you all in good health and spirits. Now onto my very newbie and basic two part question.<br /> <br /> Freeholds, where do they stand in terms of the Dreaming vs. the Autumn World? I mean from a narrative and imaginary perspective. Are freehold in the mundane world or are they situation in the Near Dreaming just beyond a portal? Also do the portals give entrance directly to Freeholds and then to the Near Dreaming or vice versus? And my very last question. Is it possible to run a story that takes place in different parts of the Dreaming ( be it Near, Deep or Far) without the character gaining too much glamour and ending up in Bedlam?<br /> <br /> I'm running my first Changeling game since the original came out all those years ago and I am running it for a group of people completely new to this type of gaming. So I want to make sure I understand how these aspects of the game work. Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T11:10:12-07:00","id":1388713,"title":"","content":"Heya there!<br /> <br /> Well, let's try and break this down step by step...<br /> <br /> Freeholds are resovoirs of glamour connected to The Waking World and Near Dreaming both that can serve as safe grounds for changelings and chimera. They have physical seemings but contain bridges/portals stepping over into chimerical reality with at least one port of access into the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> To provide an example, let's say that the city of Dunhurst has an Irish bar maintained by the Autumn Sidhe of House Fiona. The bar is open to the public and serves as a genuine bar, but changelings know the right rhymes that turn any door into a passage over into Chimerical Reality. From that side of the Dreaming, their is a specific doorway that they can use to go out into the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> It's possible to have games run significant stretches within freeholds without becoming bedlam fests, but changelings must occasionally return to the Autumn World to avoid becoming overly chimerical. I think the metric is either a week or a number of days equivalent to one's glamour rating leading to banality checks with at least a day outside the freehold to level oneself somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T23:16:19-07:00","id":1389207,"title":"","content":"Thank you, so I have been figuring it correctly. And thank you for answering my question about spending long periods of time in the Dreaming. I was hoping to run a quest in which they go to another realm. So I'll have to figure out how to pull that off.<br /> <br /> I do have another question, but I am not sure if I should post it here or start a new thread about it. It's in regards to the Chrysalis and the Saining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26140,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","user":"whelan0kkult","date":". 05-17-2020, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T23:38:45-07:00","id":1389208,"title":"","content":"Feel free to post here if you'd like or elsewhere, no worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T00:14:46-07:00","id":1389210,"title":"","content":"Ok this question is fairly simple and straight to the point. I understood that the Chrysalis is something that NEW Changelings go through. So Say you have a Troll who is 100's or even thousands of years old and perhaps has had his mortal form die a few times....does that meaning he goes through his Chrysalis and Saining each time he is born into a new mortal form? Or is that just a one time thing when he was first born thousands or years ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T00:26:58-07:00","id":1389214,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so this is a bit tricky, but let's break it down...<br /> <br /> Post-shattering, the fae soul (calling it either a soul or spirit is academically messy, but roll with me) entrenched itself into autumn reality by bonding with mortals via the Changeling Way.<br /> <br /> The spirit has the potential to manifest within any of its vessels and at the end of any vessels life it will spend a year and a day floating in an uncertain state before merging with a new form. This is what is often called fae reincarnation.<br /> <br /> Every mortal vessel undergoes the Dream Dance as they waken from the Cyrsalis and should undergo the Saining so as to ensure that they are recognized and that the new changeling can be aware of their chimerical self, given the patchy memory of each fae.<br /> <br /> However fae are most likely born from passion and dream and as such most fae spirits are millennia old with the absolute youngest being centuries or decades old. However, no matter how many times a fae takes on a vessel, it always retains its history and nature, simply understood through the cipher of the changeling and their autumn form.<br /> <br /> So while a young boy might undergo a chrysalis and become a changeling a year ago and be sained today with the troll name 'Mountain Boots', the troll's fae soul is millennia old, born from when a young proto-germanic boy looked up at a mountain on a cloudy day and imagined them as the boots of some gargantuan figure.<br /> <br /> The changeling is new, the fae soul is old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T00:53:15-07:00","id":1389217,"title":"","content":"ok, I get what you are saying, but then that means that each time a changeling is reborn into a mortal form, whoever is fostering them learns their true name. Meaning that with enough time and to many fae could learn a Changelings True name. Am I correct? That does not seem to make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T01:24:06-07:00","id":1389221,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, however Names do float through the space of changeling society with legends and what not. Ultimately though, every changeling will die a mortal death and will be reborn and they're lucky to recall their past live's mortal name, much less any True Names they had learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:17:37-07:00","id":1389318,"title":"","content":"That is very true. Alright cool, thank you so much for this conversation and helping my figure this out. These were all questions brought to me by one of my players and she had me stumped on the Saining bit. Again thank you!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:19:59-07:00","id":1389320,"title":"","content":"No worries, best of luck to ya and a lot of fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}